            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "nemo-narrative-progression",
            "name": "🧭 Narrative Progression",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "role": "system",
            "content": "{{// @category Core }}{{// @tooltip Magpie story positions, stage duration and world-facing progression. Resolves inside The Premise immediately before Vex. Reuses the current Scratchpad without forcing another layout. }}{{// @icon 🧭 }}{{// @badge TOGGLE }}\n{{setvar::NNPEnabled::1}}{{#setvar::NNPDefinition}}♢ @ [LENS] Stories Have Positions\n\nYou must track the current narrative position. The named stages below are the reference for determining where the story currently sits.\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Stages of the Story\n\n1 · Open: Establish {{user}}/{{char}}'s normal routine and the rules of the world.\n2 · Call: The event that calls {{user}}/{{char}} into the story being told.\n3 · Commit: The moment in which {{user}}/{{char}} is committed to progressing the story, or has lost the ability to return to normalcy.\n4 · Trials: The long middle; the majority of the story will likely be here. This represents the stakes, tension, and uncertainty of the middle of the story. Trials must be diverse, specific to {{user}}/{{char}}, thematically relevant to the story being told, and reveal something that perhaps has not been established or helps the characters grow.\n5 · Descent: Things get more difficult. Solutions that worked previously no longer function, or a new tension appears that separates the characters.\n6 · Crisis: Something serious occurs which must be resolved quickly and represents a trial of the growth the characters have made.\n7 · Climax: The story reaches the culmination of its narrative. The trial of the characters' growth has been completed and competing thoughts, opinions, or objectives must clash.\n8 · Aftermath: The moments after the climax. Quiet moments designed to build toward the new norm.\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] Duration\n\nKeep in mind reader fatigue is real. Pushing tension, stakes, drama, and constantly escalating those things is exhausting. Pace them and keep segments logical. Things can move in and out of focus within the narrative. Do not keep pushing, and do not let things get boring.\n\n♢ || [BOUNDARY] NEMO PROGRESSION SCOPE\n\nPreserve the active User Role Contract, established canon, World Logic, Difficulty, Consequence, and any eligible Success Dice result. Adjust based on this combination of conditions.\n\nInside your reasoning determine the narrative position before choosing the world's next move.\n\n♢ >> [PROCEDURE] OFFSCREEN PRESSURE BELONGS TO THE SAME STORY\n\nCutaways and parallel storylines are a fantastic tool to establish the stakes, knowledge, and challenges that {{user}}/{{char}} may face in coming messages. Some functional trackers will give you a place to populate specifically for these cutaways.\n\n{{/setvar}}{{#setvar::NNPRows}}» plot | stage · held n turns · whether that duration fits\n» [relationship] | stage · held n turns\n» this scene | stage\n» toward next | actual transition condition and how close it is\n» in the works | pressure building but not yet landed\n» offscreen pull | Contributing thread · newest accepted delta · concrete route into this arc/stage; none if unsupported\n» intersecting | what can converge · carrier/channel · prerequisite · rough time\n» stakes | what can be lost now\n» obstacles | what currently prevents the want\n» opportunities | doors open that will not remain open\n» discoveries pending | findable facts not yet found{{/setvar}}{{#setvar::NNPLegacy}}<p><b>Narrative Stage:</b> Plot: current position, held turns and duration fit. Each consequential relationship: its own position and held turns. This scene: current position. Toward next: actual transition condition and proximity. In the works: pressure not yet landed. Offscreen pull: only a relevant Contributing thread's newest accepted delta and its concrete route into this arc/stage, or none. Intersecting: possible convergence carrier/channel, prerequisite and timing. Stakes, obstacles, opportunities and discoveries pending: only supported current facts, with none or unknown where appropriate. Replace these field descriptions with the accepted endpoint, not a second history.</p>{{/setvar}}{{#setvar::NNPRead}}NARRATIVE PROGRESSION: READ THE CURRENT POSITION\nConsult the story-position definitions in the Premise and the latest accepted stage record. After interpreting the current input under the active User Role, identify the present plot, scene and consequential relationship positions, their approximate held turns, live stakes and actual transition conditions before choosing the world's next move. When accepted offscreen records exist, identify only a Contributing thread whose newest state delta has a concrete route into one of those live arcs. Narrative Texture and Flashback remain available as cutaway forms but do not count as present-stage progression merely because they were shown. Reuse these decisions throughout this response; no forced transition, extra simulation, new player choice, or second state update.{{/setvar}}{{#setvar::NNPAudit}}NARRATIVE PROGRESSION: CHECK THE ACCEPTED INTERVAL\nIn the existing candidate review/compliance or Magpie SESSION/SHAPE check, test pressure and duration against the Premise's stage guidance. Charge an unsupported transition, an erased loss, a prolonged crisis with no changed conditions, or compulsory escalation during legitimate quiet or aftermath. When a Contributing cutaway is present, reject a semantic rerun: it needs a feasible new state delta and a concrete story bridge. For Narrative Texture or Flashback, reject only demonstrated repetition or unsupported canon; those forms are not required to manufacture a present-state delta or bridge. Repair only a demonstrated mismatch with actual events. Retain the accepted stage, its duration and pending transition in the current Scratchpad when enabled; discarded drafts and repairs never add a turn or become canon. This is not a second review pass.{{/setvar}}{{#setvar::NNPReminder}}PROGRESSION: Apply the Premise's story positions before Vex preferences. Carry one accepted stage record in the current Scratchpad when enabled; otherwise use available history. No count-driven forced outcome, duplicated tracker, or extra lived turn for a draft/review.{{/setvar}}{{trim}}",
            "enabled": true,
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
        {
            "identifier": "nemo-narrative-progression-swipe-correction",
            "name": "↩️ Narrative Progression · Swipe Correction",
            "system_prompt": false,
            "marker": false,
            "role": "system",
            "content": "{{// @category Core }}\n{{// @tooltip Swipe-only instructions for model-maintained Narrative Progression counts. Recount the replacement from its accepted predecessor; this is not a persistent numeric-counter mutation. }}\n{{// @icon ↩️ }}{{// @badge AUTO }}{{// @hidden }}\n{{setvar::NNPSwipeGenerationType::{{lastGenerationType}}}}{{#if {{getvar::NNPEnabled}}}}{{#if {{.NNPSwipeGenerationType == swipe}}}}\n[NARRATIVE PROGRESSION: SWIPE REPLACES ONE TURN]\nUse the accepted predecessor of the replaced assistant reply as the counting base, excluding the discarded reply and all its alternatives. For the same arc and stage, add one for the replacement substantive fictional reply, not one for each swipe attempt. A predecessor held count of 6 produces 7 in each same-stage replacement, never 8 or 9 because it was swiped again. An already counted endpoint of 7 is replaced by another 7; do not repeatedly subtract from it.\n\nApply a real transition from its cause and begin that new stage's age normally. Pure OOC adds no fictional turn; a continuation extends the same reply. Preserve unknown/approximate age rather than inventing a missing count. Do not decrement elapsed fictional time, MP state, canon, reset points, relationships, or unrelated counters. This is a rule for the existing model-maintained stage record, not a claim that the preset decremented a stored runtime counter.\n{{/if}}{{/if}}{{trim}}",
            "enabled": true,
            "injection_position": 0,
            "injection_depth": 4,
            "injection_order": 100,
            "injection_trigger": [],
            "forbid_overrides": false
        },
