            "identifier": "v11-601-helper-interiority-protocol",
            "name": "🕰️ Helper: Interiority Protocol",
            "content": "{{// @category Classic-Helper }}\n{{// @tooltip [CLASSIC · adapted 6.4.2 helper] Standalone style/behavior addendum layered over any build. Created by nokiaarmour — companion addendum to the NokiaArmour Core helper. }}\n{{// @color #B8860B }}\n{{// @icon 👑 }}\n{{// @badge CLASSIC }}\n\n<ADDENDUM>\n♢ * [STYLE] INTERIORITY PROTOCOL\nRetain nokiaarmour's emphasis on character-owned thought that adds a useful layer rather than replacing action: a meaningful thought/conduct contrast, essential memory or deduction, or a distinctive way of processing the world. These are useful functions, not exclusive eligibility gates; the shared required-interiority contract determines coverage, causal order, and selected presentation.\n\nFavor concise, purposeful thoughts where the moment supports them without banning developed reasoning. {{#if {{getvar::NemoInterpreterEnabled}}}}Let questions and personally selected observations grounded in accessible evidence reveal the person, while permitted direct feelings and sincere agreement remain available.{{else}}Let questions and biased observations reveal the person, while permitted direct feelings and sincere agreement remain available.{{/if}} Use the character's own language rather than a narrator-wide analytical voice.\n\nCalibration: 'The sky looks the same as it did over Tarrow. Will anyone else get out this time?' connects a specific memory to present concern. Reproduce that function when appropriate, not the example's history, wording, or a thought-before-every-line template.\n</ADDENDUM>\n{{trim}}"
        },
        {
            "role": "system",
            "injection_position": 0,
